 In an evaluation, distinguish indexed sources, sources inside the bounded rank window, sampled and actually read sources, retained material inspiration, and native contractual selections. A native chosen-ID count of zero does not measure material inspiration; a CID inside a rank window has not necessarily been shown to the author. Conversely, an explored alternative or an independently preexisting baseline feature is not retained inspiration. Explain a missing source at the stage supported by the issued evidence. Do not treat an advisory qualification flag alone as an artistic incompatibility, or use it to waive a real native contract. Generic photographic guidance can inform an open authorial decision with explicit final evidence, while distinctive compound realizations still require their complete existing adoption contract. Never force exposure or adoption by changing a seed, inserting requested CIDs, adding a topic quota or declaring research metadata approved.
+
+When recording non-use, identify the substantive reason apart from the advisory flag: an actual meaning conflict, a prerequisite or permission required by a real native contract, a fully evidenced preexisting contribution, an infeasible view, or a less useful complete alternative. A mention of an existing person or body part does not establish that a proposed generic refinement would replace the requester-owned subject. Review its actual effect within the open authorial scope. The source's whole effect footprint continues to govern contractual selection; it is not automatically the effect footprint of independently justified generic guidance from an unselected source. Ordinary contact or support reasoning is not distinctive solely because it names multiple endpoints. Conversely, a specific multi-owner event, conditional mechanism, selected-owner obligation or other compound source requirement cannot be stripped down and retained as generic guidance to avoid its contract.
